  "notes": "Mimetic word for speaking indistinctly with the mouth barely opening, typically from hesitation or embarrassment. Also describes slow movement inside a closed mouth.\n\nUSAGE:\n- As adverb: もごもご⟦{話|はな}す→話す：00467_hanasu⟧ (to mumble)\n- With ⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: もごもご⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧ (to mumble; to fidget with the mouth)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦ぼそぼそ→ぼそぼそ：09453_bosoboso⟧: muttering — low, quiet, flat murmuring\n- ⟦もぐもぐ→もぐもぐ：05775_mogumogu⟧: munching; mumbling — emphasizes chewing/mouth movement",
